WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.300
The king's timetable, in an

2
00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:04.620
ancient Indian handbook, is not

3
00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:05.980
for the faint hearted.

4
00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:08.530
It has no free afternoons.

5
00:00:08.956 --> 00:00:10.096
The handbook is the

6
00:00:10.096 --> 00:00:12.836
Arthashastra. Tradition names

7
00:00:12.836 --> 00:00:15.696
its author as Kautilya, adviser

8
00:00:15.696 --> 00:00:17.656
to Chandragupta Maurya;

9
00:00:17.656 --> 00:00:19.576
scholars debate who wrote it,

10
00:00:19.576 --> 00:00:20.746
and when.

11
00:00:21.216 --> 00:00:23.156
It was long thought lost.

12
00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:25.556
In nineteen oh five, R.

13
00:00:25.556 --> 00:00:27.676
Shamasastry found a copy.

14
00:00:27.676 --> 00:00:29.696
His English translation appeared

15
00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:31.697
in nineteen fifteen.

16
00:00:31.897 --> 00:00:33.877
Book one, chapter nineteen

17
00:00:33.877 --> 00:00:36.237
splits the king's day into eight

18
00:00:36.237 --> 00:00:38.637
parts: accounts, the people's

19
00:00:38.637 --> 00:00:41.257
affairs, spies, the army.

20
00:00:41.257 --> 00:00:43.487
Even sleep gets a slot.

21
00:00:43.925 --> 00:00:45.825
One court rule is blunt:

22
00:00:45.825 --> 00:00:47.665
never make petitioners wait at

23
00:00:47.665 --> 00:00:48.445
the door.

24
00:00:48.445 --> 00:00:50.405
A king out of reach breeds

25
00:00:50.405 --> 00:00:52.985
confusion, discontent, and, in

26
00:00:52.985 --> 00:00:54.315
time, enemies.

27
00:00:55.012 --> 00:00:56.532
Then comes the line everyone

28
00:00:56.532 --> 00:00:59.052
remembers. In the happiness of

29
00:00:59.052 --> 00:01:01.472
his subjects lies his happiness;

30
00:01:01.472 --> 00:01:03.882
in their welfare, his welfare.

31
00:01:04.439 --> 00:01:06.639
The next line is sharper.

32
00:01:06.639 --> 00:01:08.259
Whatever pleases the king

33
00:01:08.259 --> 00:01:10.499
himself he shall not count as

34
00:01:10.499 --> 00:01:12.639
good; only what pleases his

35
00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:13.589
subjects.

36
00:01:14.274 --> 00:01:15.614
Fine words.

37
00:01:15.614 --> 00:01:17.834
The handbook still posts spies,

38
00:01:17.834 --> 00:01:19.194
just to check.

39
00:01:19.194 --> 00:01:21.054
It trusts a king's intentions,

40
00:01:21.054 --> 00:01:23.424
and keeps a second opinion.

41
00:01:24.726 --> 00:01:25.573
For GS4:

42
00:01:25.573 --> 00:01:28.006
Kautilya's ideal ruler puts duty

43
00:01:28.006 --> 00:01:30.906
first. His happiness rests on

44
00:01:30.906 --> 00:01:32.646
the people's, and he must be

45
00:01:32.646 --> 00:01:33.446
reachable.

46
00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:36.820
The timetable, by the way, still

47
00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:39.090
has no free afternoons.
